@@ -31,8 +31,15 @@ record itself. Explicit Flush, or a deliberately paused/stopped worker, may
 render on the calling thread. Tests changing options or callbacks must Flush
 first: those changes apply when records are written, not when queued.
 
-At the inherited capacity of 1,024 records, slot storage is 512 KiB per
-prepared thread, plus the reserved record and metadata. Slots are not zeroed
-at construction: reserved address space and resident memory are different.
-This capacity is not yet claimed sufficient for the realistic-load zero-drop
-requirement; ring sizing is a separate measured gate.
+The capacity is 16,384 records per prepared thread: 8 MiB of queue slots,
+plus one 512-byte severe overflow record and metadata (704 bytes total beyond
+slots on the tested macOS arm64 ABI). Slots are not zeroed at allocation:
+resident pages grow as they are used. The thread-local shared pointer and
+registry/control-block containers add their own small allocation overhead.
+
+The inherited 1,024-slot ring lost debug/info records during the full functional
+suite; its largest written overflow notice was 12,870 lines. The larger ring
+absorbs that measured burst without adding a user-facing sizing option.
+This is burst capacity, not a promise to buffer an indefinitely stalled sink.
+Sustained artificial floods may still drop; measurements must report accepted,
+dropped and actually written counts.
